Per section 4(b) of that license, the following significant changes were made to
the original work before it was redistributed under this name:

1. Local generation provider.
   Added a ComfyUI-backed generation provider (`src/core/generation-providers/`)
   so the workspace runs entirely against a local ComfyUI instance, with no
   remote account or API key. `ACTIVE_GENERATION_PROVIDER_ID` defaults to it.

2. Local model catalogue.
   Added `src/core/effects/effect-registry.ts` entries and matching workflow
   templates under `data/comfyui/workflows/` for local image, video and TTS
   models. Cloud-hosted bindings were removed from the provider catalogue.

3. Per-step generation progress.
   Added `src/core/effects/comfyui-progress.ts`, which listens on ComfyUI's
   WebSocket and surfaces step counts through the status and generation-list
   APIs; the studio feed renders a progress bar from it.

4. Windows service management.
   Added `launcher/` (a PowerShell launcher and a GUI start/stop console) plus
   documentation for running the app and ComfyUI as scheduled tasks.

5. Chinese and Japanese UI.
   Added `messages/zh.json` and `messages/ja.json`, and switched the product
   name and visual identity to 漫客工作台 / Manke Workbench as required by the
   upstream trademark policy (see docs/TRADEMARKS.md).

6. Smaller behaviour changes.
   Empty-state actions on the assets page, starting-idea thumbnails that seed the
   prompt, a faster status poll with an explicit transitional state on the
   services page, and a `Cache-Control: no-cache` header for HTML documents so a
   stale page cannot reference asset hashes from an older build.

